<title>SINGAPORE: Singapore July retail sales up 3.5 percent on year.</title>
<headline>Singapore July retail sales up 3.5 percent on year.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-08-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Singapore's July retail sales index (base 1991) rose 3.5 percent compared to a year ago, the Department of Statistics said on Friday.</p>
<p>The index rose 4.1 percent from June 1996.</p>
<p>Excluding motor vehicles, the index registered a month-on-month rise of 5.2 percent in July.</p>
<p>July retail sales were estimated at Singapore $2.00 billion. The statistics department said that year-on-year, in constant prices, the retail index rose by 4.3 percent.  </p>
<p>    Retail Sales Index (at Current Prices)   (pct change)</p>
<p>				   Month-on-Month     Yr-on-Yr</p>
<p>    Total index		    4.1		  3.5</p>
<p>    X-vehicle sales		5.2		  5.0</p>
<p>    Textiles/apparels	    6.5		 -1.1</p>
<p>    Furniture/households	 6.1		 16.9</p>
<p>    Vehicle sales		  0.4		 -1.5</p>
<p>    Petrol stations		1.6		  3.5</p>
<p>    Departments/supermarts     9.4		  0.8</p>
<p>    General provisions	   1.9		 -0.7</p>
<p>    Other retail		   1.6		 12.0</p>
